== Wave 1: Mod List

Wave 1 adds graphics enhancements, new unit packs, and faction expansions. No total overhauls — the game remains recognizable.

=== Map Improvements

#mod-panel("Strongholds Of The Samurai", "https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1507085670", oda-crimson)[
  5-part mod providing 36 historically accurate castle maps for campaign siege battles. Each settlement type and level receives a unique, hand-crafted map that replaces the generic vanilla layouts. The AI handles the complex castle designs well, but be aware of a known issue: when defending, cavalry and generals may spawn underground on some maps. Move all units inside the walls during deployment before starting the battle.

  #v(4pt)
  #set text(size: 10pt)
  - Part 1: #link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1507085670")[link]
  - Part 2: #link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1507094229")[link]
  - Part 3: #link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1507101969")[link]
  - Part 4: #link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1507106653")[link]
  - Part 5: #link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1507120263")[link]

  Last updated: September 2020. #text(fill: green)[116K+ subscribers.]
]

=== Graphics Enhancements

#mod-panel("Bullgod's Horse Texture Mod", "https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2907654155", oda-crimson)[
  Crisper, higher-quality horse textures with darker reins and improved manes. Affects all cavalry units — light, heavy, and general's bodyguard. Purely visual, no stat changes.
]

=== Campaign Map Visuals

#mod-panel("Castle Campaign Map Models", "https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2988063933", oda-crimson)[
  Replaces the generic vanilla castle models on the campaign map with detailed, tier-specific designs. Each fortress level gets a unique visual — citadels and Kyoto have their own distinct look. Visual only; does not affect battle maps or siege layouts.

