=== Immersion

#mod-panel("Campaign Unit Stealth (Vanilla)", "https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=121311886", oda-crimson)[
  Grants Kisho Ninja and Yugekitai units the ability to hide in plain sight on the campaign map, matching their battlefield stealth role. Works with vanilla units only — not compatible with third-party unit packs. For use in Sengoku and Fall of the Samurai campaigns.
]

=== Unit Packs

#mod-panel("Weierstrass Units for Vanilla", "https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1878707871", oda-crimson)[
  Adds new historically-inspired units to the vanilla roster without overhauling existing balance. Designed to integrate cleanly with the base game's unit tiers and faction identities. Part 1 of the Weierstrass unit series.

  #v(4pt)
  #set text(size: 10pt)
  - Part 1: #link("https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1878707871")[link]
]

#mod-panel("Updated Wako Units + Pirate Ports + Imperial/Black Ship", "https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2148316153", oda-crimson)[
  Overhauls the Wako pirate faction with updated unit rosters and adds new pirate port infrastructure. Also includes the Imperial Trade Ship and Black Ship units for naval variety. Builds on vanilla naval and faction systems without breaking existing balance.
]

=== Faction Expansions

#mod-panel("Recruitable Generals (No Horo)", "https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2182649204", oda-crimson)[
  Allows recruiting generals directly without the horo (the distinctive cape/balloon worn by mounted commanders). Gives you more control over your general pool while keeping recruitment costs and limits intact. Purely an immersion and roster management improvement.
]

=== Compatibility Notes

All Wave 1 mods are selected for mutual compatibility. If you experience crashes, verify:
1. Load order matches 01-setup.typ
2. No Wave 2 mods are accidentally subscribed
3. No mod from Wave 0 that conflicts is still active
